  "liner": {
   "body_md": "Mountain Goats performed a full twenty-five song set at The Toff In Town in Melbourne, Australia, on Wednesday, May 9, 2012 [1]. This concert is documented by a single audience recording titled tmg2012-05-09.aud, which runs for ninety-eight minutes [1]. The audio was taped and transferred by Christopher Jacques, providing a clear lineage for the file [1]. The setlist includes the rare track \"Counterfeit Florida Plates,\" which appears in only four archived performances [1][2]. Listeners can also hear \"Hawaiian Feeling,\" a legendary song that is the only archived performance of its kind [1][2]. The recording features \"Fall of The Star High School Running Back,\" a bustout that marks its first appearance in twenty-seven archived shows after a gap of 1,061 days [1][2]. \"Night Light\" is also noted as a first in the archive [1][2]. Other songs include \"For Charles Bronson,\" \"Old College Try,\" \"Birth of Serpents,\" \"Damn These Vampires,\" \"Jeff Davis County Blues,\" \"Hast Thou Considered The Tetrapod,\" \"Woke Up New,\" \"You Were Cool,\" \"Transcendental Youth,\" \"The Diaz Brothers,\" \"White Cedar,\" \"Palmcorder Yajna,\" \"International Small Arms Traffic Blues,\" \"Pigs That Ran Straightaway Into the Water, Triumph of,\" \"Love Love Love,\" \"Game Shows Touch Our Lives,\" \"You Or Your Memory,\" \"This Year,\" \"1 Samuel 15:23,\" \"Quito,\" and \"The Best Ever Death Metal Band In Denton\" [1]. This event is the 170th of 467 shows in the archive's collection for the performer [2]. The previous archived show took place on May 6, 2012, at The Metro [2].",
